Subject: [PATCH] feat(editor): add reference images and design documents to a
 new game
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Joinery-only, not meant for upstream: it extends the Joinery wizard.

Brief and art direction gains Design documents under Game brief and
Reference images after References. Files are added with Add documents…
and Add images… or dropped on the window (the Project Manager forwards
drops while that step shows). Each picture shows a thumbnail and a
one-line note for what to take from it, each document its name and
kind, and × takes a file off the list. A file of the wrong kind is
refused with a plain sentence.

On create the lists travel in .joinery-references.json and
.joinery-design-docs.json beside the project, never through a shell,
for joinery game apply (or joinery brief and bible without a starting
point), which checks and copies each file.
